{"id": "EUVD-2026-103654", "enisaUuid": "e162c1f8-7d61-36ce-9351-2c66f60856e1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/virtio: fix object leak when drm_gem_handle_create() fails\n\nvirtio_gpu_gem_create() owns the reference taken by\nvirtio_gpu_object_create(). On the drm_gem_handle_create() error path it\ncalls drm_gem_object_release() instead of dropping that reference.\n\ndrm_gem_object_release() is the inverse of drm_gem_object_init() and does\nnot touch the reference count or call obj->funcs->free(), so it is only\ncorrect as the last step of a destructor, as in\nvirtio_gpu_cleanup_object(). Using it here leaves the bo at refcount 1\nwith no remaining reference, so virtio_gpu_free_object() never runs and\nthe shmem pages, sg table and virtio_gpu_object are leaked. Since\nvirtio_gpu_object_create() has already set bo->created,\nVIRTIO_GPU_CMD_RESOURCE_UNREF is not queued either, leaking the host-side\nresource and the resource id.\n\ndrm_gem_handle_create_tail() drops the handle reference on all of its\ninternal error paths, so the caller only has to drop its own. Use\ndrm_gem_object_put(), matching the success path below.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:36", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/13423a058187c2039aa8cb235c916be4477221b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/687be2f8b5e0e0ca9a7028f8f6413d0ed3fbb9dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/264ae8ac8fd625b6c118baf16c111adeee2ec632", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2edd2d78d2cf8446de017adec9598feefed3297", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/372e9c3d45f664a2c000427ccbf6cdc2f99b3170", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a93dce15dfef200c346b050a2acbed516cc62706", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f75066c79d1eec453c0d386ef8636873d1e11f2c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36570ef2244cc4d7563b1f0157bc0f032498638c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98609", "GHSA-4mj5-5wcx-f4jj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "110e51eb-fff4-3409-b536-8c936442f45d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "158abd4b-fdd1-3a61-98fb-d9a49ecb5bc3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dc5698e80cf724770283e10414054662bdf6ccfa <13423a058187c2039aa8cb235c916be4477221b7"}, {"id": "2cf0aed1-5ff0-373f-a3a7-a8a05194f6c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dc5698e80cf724770283e10414054662bdf6ccfa <372e9c3d45f664a2c000427ccbf6cdc2f99b3170"}, {"id": "2e472207-fc60-3fff-ad91-a0eed5ad6081", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "31b1a9ed-c88d-3c2d-bd46-6afa7d207b73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dc5698e80cf724770283e10414054662bdf6ccfa <f75066c79d1eec453c0d386ef8636873d1e11f2c"}, {"id": "529b625d-8fde-3d0a-a639-87ebd3366552", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dc5698e80cf724770283e10414054662bdf6ccfa <e2edd2d78d2cf8446de017adec9598feefed3297"}, {"id": "55ec2741-8c01-3ff4-8c6e-4407298a3902", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.2"}, {"id": "89f55e73-9012-3c94-8ddf-f0f423b59ca2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8c400cb7-b5b0-3438-9d4f-1c43a0286053", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "a2586162-853d-3d9f-a3d4-38f73ec95a59", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dc5698e80cf724770283e10414054662bdf6ccfa <264ae8ac8fd625b6c118baf16c111adeee2ec632"}, {"id": "bb2a66bf-19f9-36da-ac7b-52002c0d869f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dc5698e80cf724770283e10414054662bdf6ccfa <687be2f8b5e0e0ca9a7028f8f6413d0ed3fbb9dc"}, {